  "investigation_notes": "Upload failure investigation - evidence based:\n\n**Current state:**\n- `incidentlab-app-1` `running` `Up 11 seconds` (E1,E12,E5) - running=true, restart_count=0 (E5)\n- `incidentlab-db-1` `exited` `Exited (0) 8 seconds ago` (E1,E12) - running=false, exit_code=0 (E6)\n- App `/health` `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2)\n\nApp is running but unhealthy. DB dependency is down.\n\n**Root cause vs symptom:**\n- Symptom: app unhealthy (E2 503) -> uploads stop working.\n- Root cause: database container stopped, not app storage failure. Both containers on same network `incidentlab_default` (E5,E6), so app lost its dependency when db exited.\n\n**Ruled out with evidence:**\n\n- Disk full on data volume: `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent 9.0`, `available_mb 410.6`, `inode_use_percent 0.2` (E3) - not full.\n- Disk full on root: `/` `use_percent 6.8`, `available_mb 91409.1`, `inode_use_percent 1.5` (E10) - not full.\n- Permissions on uploads: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is_dir true, owner 1000:1000, mode 0755, app_uid 1000, app_gid 1000, `app_user_can_write true` (E4) - writable.\n- Permissions on parent: `/srv/lab-data` same ownership/mode, `app_user_can_write true` (E11) - writable.\n- Mount missing / read-only: app has bind `source /srv/lab-data -> destination /data rw true` (E5) - present and writable.\n- OOMKill: app `oom_killed false` (E5), db `oom_killed false` (E6) - not OOM.\n- App crash loop: app `exit_code 0`, `error null` (E5), `restart_count 0` (E5).\n\n**Why db stopped:**\n- DB `started_at 2026-10-29T15:57:44Z`, `finished_at 2026-10-29T15:57:52Z`, `exit_code 0`, `error null` (E6)\n- Events (E9): `db start` at 15:57:44, `health_status: healthy` at 15:57:49 after `pg_isready` exec_die 0, `app start` at 15:57:49, then `db kill, stop, die exit 0` at 15:57:52 - 3 seconds after app start.\n- Pattern is graceful `kill/stop/die 0`, not crash, not OOM (E6), not failed health check prior to stop (E9 shows healthy).\n- Logs unavailable for both containers (E7,E8 `this data source is unavailable`), so DB internal error cannot be confirmed from logs.\n\nConclusion: Uploads failing because app is unhealthy (E2) due to dependency `incidentlab-db-1` being stopped/exited (E1,E6,E12). Storage, permissions, disk space, OOM and mounts ruled out by E3,E4,E5,E6,E10,E11. No repair attempted.\n",
